{"duration_api_ms":27718,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7f0812df-0d68-4886-afd2-431ed949609a","total_cost_usd":0.9842837999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":105279,"cache_read_input_tokens":400679,"output_tokens":3095,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1162},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":105279,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":646,"cache_read_input_tokens":201097,"cache_creation_input_tokens":73394,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":73394},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3095,"cacheReadInputTokens":400679,"cacheCreationInputTokens":105279,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9842837999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1162,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":2,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote `labels/coder-1.json` (codebook 0.4, coder slot 1). It has one row, `egi-draft-a1v2`, and I coded it **rung 2: \"Forbid rules that require schools to tell parents.\"**\n\n- **The vote:** Zbur voted Aye on AB 1955 (2023-24) on 2024-06-27. That was the Assembly's concurrence vote, its final vote on the chaptered text. The tally was 61–16, so about 21% voted No and the near-unanimous rule does not apply. The vote is within his current term.\n- **The provision:** I quoted Section 220.5(a) as the `provision_quote`. It bars districts, county offices and charter schools from enacting or enforcing any policy that would require staff to disclose a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That matches rung 2.\n- **Why not rung 1:** Section 220.3 only says staff are not *required* to disclose. Nothing in the bill requires staff to keep the information from parents, so it does not reach rung 1.\n- **Why not rungs 3–5:** the bill requires no notice to parents and no parental permission.\n- **Sources:** `rests_on` holds both passages: the vote page (with the actor and tally quotes) and the bill text (with the provision quote).\n\n**Judgement call:** I treated the bill as single-subject. It also has a parent-resources section and an anti-retaliation section, but all three concern LGBTQ pupils' rights, and I relied only on Section 220.5. A reviewer who reads it as multi-subject would downgrade the vote to direction only.\n\nThe bill text lists Zbur as a principal coauthor. I mentioned this only in a note and did not code it as a sponsorship record, because the bill was introduced on a different subject and the codebook says sponsorship evidences the bill as filed.\n\nNo source of his own words was provided, so the row has no quotes. `needs_source` is empty.","ttft_ms":11435,"type":"result","duration_ms":31406,"uuid":"a9ee51fa-3f07-403d-852f-82e115320723","ttft_stream_ms":967,"time_to_request_ms":175,"first_content_frame_ms":968,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
